# Every text file is LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every platform. Without this, a
# Windows checkout (Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, and the windows-latest runner uses it) turns
# every line ending into CRLF, and the tests that compare a file with a string written in a test, with the
# bytes of a starter template, with the output of the formatter or with a byte offset fail for that reason
# alone. The scaffold and site/ are copied into projects and published, so they must be LF as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes, never converted, never diffed as text. `text=auto` already detects these, and the fixtures that
# compare a copy with its original byte for byte (test/site/starter.test.ts) must never depend on a guess.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.tgz binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
